From a662908d4ed4269a8867a005e5be7e1cd122f2e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 16:48:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 02/31] android: Support the software ISP as an Android camera

Make a camera that relies on the software ISP, such as those of the
Samsung Galaxy Tab A 10.1 (2016, Exynos 7870), usable through the
Android HAL.

HAL:
- The software ISP outputs XRGB8888: convert it to NV12 with libyuv
  for the YUV and implementation-defined streams, and encode JPEG
  directly from it (JCS_EXT_BGRX), thumbnails included.
- The software ISP has a single output: derive every further YUV
  stream from the largest one, centre-cropped and scaled.
- Allocate the intermediate RGB buffers from a cached dma-buf heap:
  CPU access to uncached gralloc buffers makes the NV12 conversion too
  slow for preview.
- Describe a BLOB buffer as NV12, and place the JPEG blob header at
  the gralloc width of the buffer rather than at its dma-buf length,
  which the allocator may round up.
- Ask libcamera for the sensor's native orientation, as Android
  applies the rotation itself.
- Size the internal buffers by the bytes per pixel of the format
  written to them.
- Add debug properties for the log levels and the number of debayering
  threads.
- In the AIDL session, free the output release fence instead of
  freeing the input one twice.

libcamera:
- Debayer 2-line Bayer patterns on several threads (6 by default),
  from a cached copy of the frame and into per-thread memory copied
  out in bulk. This halves the processing time of a 1632x1228 frame on
  a Cortex-A53.
- Open DMA heaps read-only: DMA_HEAP_IOCTL_ALLOC does not need write
  access, and Android makes /dev/dma_heap/system 0444.
- Add sensor properties for the SR259 and the S5K4H5YC.

Assisted-by: LLM
